{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494080-would-ctd-have-the-same-appeal-if-it-was-not-part-of-the-wod","id":1494080,"title":"Would CTD have the same appeal if it was NOT part of the WoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-01T05:47:47-07:00","id":1494080,"title":"Would CTD have the same appeal if it was NOT part of the WoD?","content":"One of the things that attracted me in CTD was the superficial dissonance it presented compared to resto of the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> I wanted to see what this colorful world who seemed to be full of wonder has to offer compared to vampire, mage, werewolf. Could it hold a candle to these games? Or was it childish like some claimed? This juxtaposition seemed to make CTD even more interesting.<br /> <br /> Discovering is surreal melancholic horror and seeing how it was still a horror game was fascinating. CTD has a lot of merit on it own right.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I was thinking, if CTD was published by another publisher, if it had no connection to WoD at all, and I really mean NO connection, not a &quot;crossovers not advised&quot; would it have become as well regarded as it is? Would it be as good as it is?<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel like the apparent contrast of CTD with the rest of WoD is one of it's biggest selling points, and frankly, makes it a little more charming too.<br /> <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 10-01-2022, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T05:57:34-07:00","id":1494081,"title":"","content":"Frankly, CTD has barely any connection to the larger WoD already, a lot of people don't like it because it feels so disconnected from the rest of WoD while others love it precisely for this, making it an independent property wouldn't change much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T08:07:06-07:00","id":1494083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494080-would-ctd-have-the-same-appeal-if-it-was-not-part-of-the-wod?p=1494081#post1494081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, CTD has barely any connection to the larger WoD already, a lot of people don't like it because it feels so disconnected from the rest of WoD while others love it precisely for this, making it an independent property wouldn't change much.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is interesting, because I think CTD actually has a lot of connections? Of course, It's all a question of point of view.<br /> <br /> <br /> Changeling and werewolf, are, I risk saying, the most connected games of all WoD. No other game has such deep connections. Some of legendary kinfolk heroes were actually fae blooded. The Fiona x Fianna relationship is just the tip of the iceberg, a lot of tribes have good relationships with specific houses or kiths.<br /> <br /> The nunnehi have access to totems that work just like WtA totems and have a certain connection with the umbra.<br /> <br /> There is a changing breed that was enslaved by the sidhe (the ceilican) for hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> Danu is literally one of the WtA totems,<br /> <br /> The high lord of house balor is protected by a pack of black spiral dancers. Etc <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T08:50:23-07:00","id":1494088,"title":"","content":"imo Changeling the Dreaming, despite its flower-child reputation, is pretty thoroughly defined by its status as a member of the World of Darkness gamelines.<br /> <br /> For one thing, the game shares a number of the design and narrative philosophies of the other games. From a mechanics perspective it obviously had the Storyteller system but I don\u2019t think that\u2019s as important as the other WoD signature: templates. The WoD developed templates as a sort of class-without-classes. It was inevitable that WoD was gonna be compared to D&amp;D and while selling itself as a game for those less interested in number crunching and more interested in storytelling, it recognized that classes had an innate gaming utility: they told you what to do and how you do it. WoD\u2019s answer to the class were their templates. Clans for vampires, Tribe/Auspice/Breed for werewolves, traditions for mages, etc; templates worked. They allowed you to quickly present a certain package of themes, an in-universe history, a set of tools, and various crunch &amp; fluff tidbits to achieve for the Storytelling system what classes had achieved for D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> But CtD wasn\u2019t just that imo. It also had strong thematic ties to the other games from the beginning. Like the rest Changeling has the motif of a romantic golden age for the world which has been lost to the corruption of time (like Werewolf or Mage), the notion that the magic of the world is on the retreat (again like Werewolf or Mage), and that the world of Changeling was distinctly worse somehow then our own (like all World of Darkness lines in theory). Furthermore imo behind the apparently bright facade Changeling has the potential to tell stories that are more depressing or tragic then wraith or vampire (not that it does so implicitly but that it has the tools at hand to do so well from time to time). Like those games Changelings exist in a constant state of existential siege as their selves are corroded by forces largely outside their control and which are synonymous with the state of our fallen world, but unlike the Vampires with Golconda or the Wraith with Transcendence, the changeling has no hope of escape. They can only try to hold back the clock while slowly dissolving into dissociation until they lose knowledge of their self or are lost utterly to madness and nightmares; and in a different sort of horror then what the other lines experience, their comrades are forced to watch in horror as their one-time friend not only forgets them but forgets themselves and becomes lost to their very way of life.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t pretend that the game is to everyone\u2019s fancy, but I don\u2019t think that one can reasonably claim that Changeling does not carry several of the traditional signatures of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com