&amp; fluff tidbits to achieve for the Storytelling system what classes had achieved for D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> But CtD wasn\u2019t just that imo. It also had strong thematic ties to the other games from the beginning. Like the rest Changeling has the motif of a romantic golden age for the world which has been lost to the corruption of time (like Werewolf or Mage), the notion that the magic of the world is on the retreat (again like Werewolf or Mage), and that the world of Changeling was distinctly worse somehow then our own (like all World of Darkness lines in theory). Furthermore imo behind the apparently bright facade Changeling has the potential to tell stories that are more depressing or tragic then wraith or vampire (not that it does so implicitly but that it has the tools at hand to do so well from time to time). Like those games Changelings exist in a constant state of existential siege as their selves are corroded by forces largely outside their control and which are synonymous with the state of our fallen world, but unlike the Vampires with Golconda or the Wraith with Transcendence, the changeling has no hope of escape. They can only try to hold back the clock while slowly dissolving into dissociation until they lose knowledge of their self or are lost utterly to madness and nightmares; and in a different sort of horror then what the other lines experience, their comrades are forced to watch in horror as their one-time friend not only forgets them but forgets themselves and becomes lost to their very way of life.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t pretend that the game is to everyone\u2019s fancy, but I don\u2019t think that one can reasonably claim that Changeling does not carry several of the traditional signatures of the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have never been a fan of dreaming (lost is more of my jam) but I really doubt that it could be more depressing than Wraith, I played in a game that used the holocaust supplement and it is to this day one of the most depressing thing I have ever played, Changeling just can't compare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T09:54:38-07:00","id":1494096,"title":"","content":"Like I said, it\u2019s not a universal rule. Like what you mentioned, there are obvious exceptions. My point was simply that CtD is capable of far more tragedy then it\u2019s sometimes given credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T10:01:03-07:00","id":1494097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1494080-would-ctd-have-the-same-appeal-if-it-was-not-part-of-the-wod?p=1494096#post1494096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, it\u2019s not a universal rule. Like what you mentioned, there are obvious exceptions. My point was simply that CtD is capable of far more tragedy then it\u2019s sometimes given credit.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how many play it like that though? The game was from it's inception described as a less dark entry in WoD, you can try to extrapolate more depressing aspects but basically everything in that book points to happier stories than the rest of WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T11:37:06-07:00","id":1494105,"title":"","content":"This may simply be an agree to disagree moment. People can play the game however they like, but the material is there. Heck there are explicit rules for becoming Undone or entering Bedlam and the setting has similar themes of the world being fallen and the looming death of magic as many of the others did.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t claim to say that Changeling is a perfect game or that it\u2019s for everyone, but I also don\u2019t think it would be fair to describe it as unrecognizable when compared to other WoD gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T13:28:19-07:00","id":1494108,"title":"","content":"OK.... so getting back to the opening question:<br /> <br /> While from a strictly financial perspective CtD might have needed being part of the WoD to get the audience it did (though I doubt that), from a thematic and design perspective I feel that on net being part of the WoD <b>hurts</b> CtD.<br /> <br /> All of the five original splats started in the &quot;Worlds&quot; of Darkness era where the games where all meant to be separate but thematically overlapping worlds. When 2e started to push it into the &quot;World&quot; of Darkness where everyone coexisted in one setting even if they tended to keep to their own corners of it, CtD suffered significantly from this change (to the point of getting cancelled along with Wraith).<br /> <br /> You don't need CtD to be part of the WoD to benefit from the mechanical lessons of the WoD, or to be a thematic juxtaposition. Trinity, Exalted, and Scion all used the same base mechanics, and took things in very different thematic directions than the WoD.<br /> <br /> I think that if we had an equivalent to Ars Magica for CtD: this would have been more clearly the case. If we had a standalone &quot;cousin&quot; game about the changelings, that doesn't have to worry about mechanical consistency with other games, or bending its needs to make the settings quasi-compatible, you'd see a much stronger and less tonally confusing game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T16:58:21-07:00","id":1494112,"title":"","content":"C: the D has great charms, I like it better than C: the L, but I see C: the L having the more powerful metaphor at its core. The Dreaming is based in a romantic concept of childhood and the loss of innocence. The Lost is about victims learning to be survivors. <br /> <br /> Like M: the Ascension, C: the Lost can be reset anywhere or anywhen. None of the other White Wolf/Onyx Path games really have this. All of the games have setting chrome that's fixed in time. But neither M: the Ascension nor C: the Lost are bound by those limits. Still C: the Dreaming is endlessly charming. It could very easily survive as a totally independent game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}